cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the EFO-Plutchik ontology module, please cite it as below."
title: "EFO-Plutchik: an EFO-compatible ontology module for Plutchik's wheel of emotions"
abstract: >-
  An Emotion Frame Ontology (EFO) compatible module formalizing Plutchik's
  wheel of emotions. Release 0.5.0 has 48 emotion individuals — 8 basic
  emotions, 16 intensity variants and all 24 dyads (primary, secondary and
  tertiary) — with the 4 opposition pairs, the geometry of the wheel, a
  vocabulary for valence/arousal/dominance readings, English and Japanese
  labels, and two documented mappings from dataset labels (SemEval-2018,
  GoEmotions) to the theory. It includes derivation rules for inferring
  compound-emotion occurrences from intensity readings and a machine-checkable
  validation layer (SHACL shapes, SPARQL competency questions, OWL-RL
  consistency).
date-released: "2026-11-14"
type: dataset
